Found while working k54: prepareNodeBridge skips npm install whenever node_modules exists. A timed-out or Ctrl-C-aborted install (k54 added a 5-minute deadline and cancellation) can leave a partial node_modules, so the next start skips the install; the smoke test then fails on the missing module and the WARN tells the user to delete the folder by hand. Fix: a completion marker written after a successful install (or compare against package-lock), so an interrupted install reruns. cmd/launcher/bridge.go, Linux-testable with a fake npm.

**Also (from k107):** the comment at cmd/launcher/bridge.go:159-160 says the smoke test runs in a job 'like every process the launcher spawns' — the short-lived taskkill/pkill (lifecycle.go killCrashReporter) and reg query (internal/config/engine.go regQuery) helpers run without one. Tighten the comment in the same pass.

Decision 2026-11-21 (main agent): a completion marker inside node_modules, written only after a successful npm install; node_modules without the marker gets npm install again (no deletion). An offline user whose complete node_modules predates the marker must not lose the bridge: if that install fails, the smoke test decides, and a passing smoke test writes the marker. Plus the job-comment fix at bridge.go:159-160. Bundled with k117 and k119 (one worker, disjoint files).

