Decision on review finding 1 (main agent, not the maintainer): no automatic move-aside of an unmarked node_modules. The launcher keeps deleting nothing, and a rename of node_modules on Windows fails on locked files anyway. Instead: (1) the marker is written only after the smoke test passes, on every path, including a successful npm install. So a partial tree that npm calls "up to date" is never locked in. (2) When the smoke test fails for a node_modules that existed before this start, the abort log names the sure fix: delete node_modules in <dir> and start again, because npm install can report a partial tree as up to date. README troubleshooting item 3 says the same. (3) Finding 2: the wording becomes "the launcher deletes nothing; npm itself may remove extraneous packages", and the "left as it was" comment is corrected. (4) Finding 3: tests for a timeout over an existing node_modules, a failed marker write and a package without dependencies. Also: the k117 positive control and the k119 ErrDot nit. Back to the worker.

